ff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:37"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"27"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"2968772","displayName":"Filip Forsberg","shortName":"F. Forsberg"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"4316983","displayName":"Blake Lizotte","shortName":"B. Lizotte"}}]},{"id":"401892757000000760","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Nils Hoglander Wrist Shot saved by Sergei Murashov","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:40"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"27"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4565263","displayName":"Nils Hoglander","shortName":"N. Hoglander"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"5188366","displayName":"Sergei Murashov","shortName":"S. Murashov"},"type":"saver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1834","fullName":"Bridgestone Arena","address":{"city":"Nashville","state":"TN","zipCode":"37250","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1834.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":17487,"officials":[{"fullName":"Chris Schlenker","displayName":"Chris Schlenker","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Andrew Smith","displayName":"Andrew Smith","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Brandon Schrader","displayName":"Brandon Schrader","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Julien Fournier","displayName":"Julien Fournier","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Struble and Marchessault lead the Predators to a 4-3 win over the Penguins","description":"— Jayden Struble and Jonathan Marchessault each had a goal and an assist to lead the Nashville Predators to a 4-3 victory over the Pittsburgh Penguins on Saturday.","story":"NASHVILLE, Tenn. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4565269/jayden-struble\">Jayden Struble</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2967072/jonathan-marchessault\">Jonathan Marchessault</a> each had a goal and an assist to lead the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/nsh/nashville-predators\">Nashville Predators</a> to a 4-3 victory over the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-penguins\">Pittsburgh Penguins</a> on Saturday. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/2968772/filip-forsberg\">Filip Forsberg</a> and Reid Schaeffer also scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3042109/juuse-saros\">Juuse Saros</a> made 21 saves for the Predators, who won for the eighth time in 10 games. Struble broke a 3-all tie at 3:31 of the third period on a tap-in from just outside the crease off a pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5037/steven-stamkos\">Steven Stamkos</a>, who has a point in five straight. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4063401/samuel-girard\">Samuel Girard</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5077308/andrei-kuzmenko\">Andrei Kuzmenko</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697405/hendrix-lapierre\">Hendrix Lapierre</a> scored and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5188366/sergei-murashov\">Sergei Murashov</a> made 25 saves for the Penguins, who have lost four of five and eight of 10 (2-7-1).\n\n\r\n              Girard scored the first goal at 3:58 of the opening period on a slap shot from above the left circle that deflected off Stamkos' stick before beating Saros high to the far side.\n\n\r\n              Kuzmenko made it 2-0 with 3:42 remaining in the first, after skating through the slot and beating Saros with a wrist shot for his first goal of the season.\n\n\r\n              Marchessault halved the Pittsburgh lead with 2:34 left in the period on a one-timer from the left side.\n\n\r\n              Since missing seven games with a lower-body injury, Marchessault has scored in consecutive games.\n\n\r\n              Saros was replaced by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4393408/justus-annunen\">Justus Annunen</a> briefly in the first after having an issue with a skate blade. Annunen stopped both shots he faced in 2:07 of ice time before Saros returned near the midpoint of the first.\n\n\r\n              Forsberg made it 2-all at 2:25 of the second, snapping a wrist shot from the left faceoff dot that snuck under Murashov’s blocker.\n\n\r\n              Schaeffer’s goal at 6:22 of the second gave Nashville its first lead.\n\n\r\n              Lapierre tied it at 3 with 6:33 remaining in the second when his wrist shot from the right side through traffic beat Saros on the far side.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Penguins: Visit the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/dal/dallas-stars\">Dallas Stars</a> on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              Predators: Play at Dallas on Wednesday. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-22T02:04:31Z"}}